  "title": "Lockstep Gantry",
  "rules": [
    "Grip the two handles two cells from the beam center. Both carriers must choose the same direction or quarter turn.",
    "The beam occupies three real cells. Translation costs one shared pressure unit; rotation costs two and needs a clear 5x5 swept square.",
    "A free worker exactly at the winch pumps three charge units, capped at ten, and refreshes the shutter to four turns.",
    "The shutter timer decreases before movement. Closing on a worker or beam cell causes a terminal jam.",
    "The center aperture is narrow; an open northern route at y=1 uses more movement. Workers and cargo can obstruct each other.",
    "Deliver a horizontal beam to center [10,4]. Every live turn costs 0.01; pumping costs its worker another 0.02.",
    "All roles receive +8 on delivery or -5 on a jam. The public scene is the actual state; witness scripts have not been run."
  ],
